            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Here are six integer cards: (+ 1), (+ 7), (+ 18), (– 5), (– 2), (– 9). You can pick any of these and make an expression using addition(s) and subtraction(s). Here is an expression: (+18)+(+1)–(+7) – (–2) which gives a value (+14). Now, pick cards and make an expression such that its value is closer to (–   30)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.37,
            0.884,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. The sum of two positive integers is always positive but a (positive integer) – (positive integer) can be positive or negative. What about a. (positive) – (negative) b. (positive) + (negative) c. (negative) + (negative) d. (negative) – (negative) e. (negative) – (positive) f. (negative) + (positive)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.209,
            0.484,
            0.884,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. This string has a total of 100 tokens arranged in a particular pattern. What is the value of the string?"
